### Central Thesis

Freddie Mercury was an Enneagram Type 4w3 who hand-built "Freddie Mercury" as a pretence, guarded the person underneath, and withdrew when hurt — and every major life episode (boarding school, offstage shyness, Mary Austin, Munich, Live Aid, the four-year silence) is that one mechanism running.

The thread is genuinely strong: every section serves the thesis, the intro's promises (gala, mirrors, Marsh's accusation, "a title he picked for himself") all pay off, and the ending closes on the same wall the cold open built. This draft had already been through fresh-eyes and second-pass work, and it shows.

